From 8c365b9dedd5619bf4878ca7d0c697637e0e5be1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Pray <nickwpray@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 16:09:25 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fork: volume meter bars trade off; add mini size

The three bars now share one height budget set by the volume. A drifting
focus decides how the budget is split, so when one bar rises the others
drop and the peak moves between bars. Silence keeps the idle pulse, muted
stays flat, and reduced motion follows volume only. Adds a `mini` variant
for the voice strip, and drops useUnistyles() from the meter.

The volume-meter design now shows the mini size and speech-like input.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
